    cues: ['Sprint dates, one set: docs/agile/definition-of-done.md “Done ladder per sprint”: Sprint 1 1–12 Sep, Sprint 2 15–26 Sep, Sprint 3 28 Sep–9 Oct, Sprint 4 12–23 Oct; dates follow the progress reports where they exist (Sprint 2: docs/sprint2-progress-report.typ L81, L118, the same period as the burndown on slide 8).', 'Ladder: EPAT 01 Agile p26 (coded → tested → integrated → releasable → released). Placing each sprint on it is our own reading of the evidence, not a course rating. Basis, the same for every sprint: the sprint goal’s increment; integrated = merged to dev with all required checks green, releasable = demonstrated on deployed dev (sprint-03/plan.md §8 “on dev” rule), released = promoted to and running in production (SWE5001 only, from Sprint 4; Stripe test mode). The footnote’s basis and the four placements are on one page: docs/agile/definition-of-done.md#done-ladder-per-sprint (current list: #current-definition-of-done-sprint-4).', 'Sprint 1 (1–12 Sep, #49): backend pipeline live on dev 5 Sep with health check and rollback; frontend not started (Sprint 1 report). Sprint 2 (15–26 Sep, #93): 9 of 11 stories, 134 of 150 h; frontend live 22 Sep; Checkout and scheduling off on dev (Sprint 2 report). Sprint 3 (28 Sep–9 Oct, #232): 117 of 150 h; review records the goal as not met on dev (sprint-03/review.md); DoD rule "on dev means demonstrated on deployed dev" (sprint-03/plan.md §8). Sprint 4 (12–23 Oct, #465): released on SWE5001 production: promotion PR #574 merged 20 Oct, deploy run 39435280952 green with the smoke suite passing against the production CloudFront at 14:31 UTC, release digests in SSM /blocbuy/swe5001/release/* (AWS read-only, 23 Oct); the SWE5001 runtime is brought up for sessions and torn down after (infra/swe5001/README.md; no ECS cluster on 23 Oct), and served the 20–21 Oct sessions including the SWE5001 talk. Stripe stays in test mode there. SWE5006 dev: releasable for paid START and the expiry refund (PR #664, 23 Oct; assumed merged by 26 Oct); a second buyer’s JOIN (#590) is not shown, so not the whole goal. SWE5006 itself has no production (#226).', 'Retro → change: Sprint 1 retro (Sprint 1 report: no burndown or story points) → dated day logs and the scheduled board snapshot to docs/agile/metrics/ from 17 Sep (Sprint 2 report, "Acting on the Sprint 1 retrospective"). Sprint 2 retro (Sprint 2 report: ≈ 10,000-line Stripe slice, cliff burndown) → sprint-03/plan.md §8: PRs under ~1,500 lines, remaining hours in the estimate field, mid-sprint check 2 Oct. Sprint 3 retro not written (#451): the only recorded action is sprint-04/plan.md §7 (owners update the estimate field; the mid-sprint check verifies it). Sprint 4 retro due 23 Oct. {{FILL:Sprint 3 and Sprint 4 retro rows (open items 5, 6)}}', 'One or two improvements per sprint follows the EPAT retrospective template (SCRUM_Process_Team01.xlsx, "Focus on 1 - 2 improvements").'],
